<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azcapotzalco</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azcapotzalco was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanec</a> state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a>, which dominated the region in the late fourteenth and early fifteenth centuries. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> were initially its tributaries. In 1428 Tenochtitlan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texcoco">Texcoco</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlacopan">Tlacopan</a> defeated Azcapotzalco and formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Triple Alliance</a> that became the Aztec Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/azcapotzalco.jpg" alt="Azcapotzalco" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ProtoplasmaKid · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Avenida_Azcapotzalco.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
